cgwatch (0.3.4-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: the release workflow now also publishes an (unsigned) flat apt
    repository to the gh-pages branch, so the package can be installed and
    upgraded via apt:
      deb [trusted=yes] https://jeroen404.github.io/cgwatch ./
  * Fix the Homepage field (was a stale github.com/jack/... URL).

 -- Jeroen <jeroen@404.eu>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 18:25:25 +0200

cgwatch (0.3.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Plasma widget: stop the "Add service" candidate list from resetting its
    scroll position and selection on every poll. The list was backed by a
    var-array model reassigned whenever any field changed (including the
    live memory usage that updates every second); it now uses a ListModel
    reconciled in place (keyed on unit, structural changes frozen while the
    add page is open), matching the cgroup list's existing rebuild pattern.

 -- Jeroen <jeroen@404.eu>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 17:40:49 +0200

cgwatch (0.3.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix the Plasma widget slowly pegging plasmashell at 100% CPU. Each poll
    used a unique per-poll nonce in the executable-DataSource command; the
    dataengine's QQmlOpenMetaObject grows a property per distinct source key
    and never shrinks, so the O(N) meta-object rebuild on every poll crept
    toward 100% over hours of uptime. The nonce is now stable per widget
    instance, keeping the source set at size 1. (The earlier 0.3.1 compact
    gauge fix addressed a different, mistaken hypothesis; this is the real
    root cause, found via gdb + a Plasma5Support DataSource A/B repro.)

 -- Jeroen <jeroen@404.eu>  Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:49:24 +0200

cgwatch (0.3.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix the Plasma widget pegging plasmashell at 100% CPU: the compact
    memory gauge read its layout-managed width back into the panel's
    size, a silent QtQuick.Layouts feedback loop. Also bump the widget's
    metadata Version (was stuck at 0.1.0, shown in the About dialog).

 -- Jeroen <jeroen@404.eu>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:35:53 +0200

